WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.237 --> 00:00:02.700
- [Lady] The Biden administration
is nearing a decision

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.290
on student loan forgiveness

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.630
an issue that could affect
millions of Americans

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:09.218
and influence the coming
midterm elections.

00:00:09.218 --> 00:00:11.490
- No matter what he ends up deciding,

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:13.740
Biden will be taking
a major political risk

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.477
whether he decides to cancel
large amounts of student debt,

00:00:16.477 --> 00:00:20.190
$10,000 worth of student debt
or no student debt at all,

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:22.110
it's going to anger somebody.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:24.120
And it's unclear whether that somebody

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.680
will be voting in November.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.620
- [Lady] Biden has already
ruled out for giving $50,000

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.890
per student borrower, but has
shown support for legislation

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.440
eliminating up to $10,000 in debt.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.470
Still some legal experts and economists

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.210
say the administration needs a plan

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.280
that will stand up to legal challenges

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:44.490
and avoid contributing to
record high inflation rates.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:47.154
As the debate over mass student
loan forgiveness continues.

00:00:47.154 --> 00:00:49.410
What are some of the key challenges

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.513
complicating Biden's final decision?

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.070
- So rather than taking
a stroke of the pen

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:59.070
and saying all student debt is canceled,

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:01.620
Biden has instead used existing powers

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:03.660
that the Federal government already has

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.490
for disabled borrowers,

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:07.590
for students who have been defrauded,

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:09.630
for people who work in public service.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:13.200
As Biden considers, whether to
cancel debt on a mass scale,

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:17.340
he has to juggle legal,
political and economic fallout

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.260
that might result from
that kind of decision.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.630
- [Lady] One concern tied to
mass student loan forgiveness

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.644
is inflation.

00:01:22.644 --> 00:01:25.020
Some economists warn debt cancellation

00:01:25.020 --> 00:01:27.090
could intensify price pressures

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:30.690
at a time when inflation is at
its highest level in 40 years

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.320
with an 8.6% annual rate as of May.

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.810
- There are worries that
canceling student debt

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:40.530
on a mass scale could exacerbate
problems with inflation

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:43.410
because it would give
borrowers more spending power

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:45.600
which they would then
use to purchase goods

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:47.160
and drive up inflation further

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:49.020
in a supply constrained economy.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:50.460
In order to prevent that,

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.860
the Biden administration is
looking at these lower levels

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:56.520
of debt forgiveness which
would be less inflationary.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.550
- [Lady] Depending on what
forgiveness policy Biden lands on

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.820
the price tag could range
anywhere from 321 billion

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.040
for $10,000 per borrower

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:07.500
all the way up to about $1.6 trillion

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.720
if all student debt is canceled.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:12.540
Eliminating all Federal student
debt could raise inflation

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:15.478
by .37 to .5 percentage points.

00:02:15.478 --> 00:02:16.890
That's according to the committee

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.020
for a responsible Federal budget,

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:21.583
an independent, non-partisan, non-profit,

00:02:21.583 --> 00:02:24.900
but some economists say a
smaller scale forgiveness program

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:27.658
could have less of an
impact on inflation rates.

00:02:27.658 --> 00:02:30.960
Biden is also considering
limiting the program to borrowers

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.685
who make less than $125,000 a year

00:02:33.685 --> 00:02:35.314
according to white house officials.

00:02:35.314 --> 00:02:38.737
- They're considering putting
an income threshold in place

00:02:38.737 --> 00:02:42.810
so that only lower income
borrowers will benefit

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.700
as opposed to higher income borrowers

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.410
who may still have student loans,

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:49.140
but are in a much better
position to pay them off.

00:02:49.140 --> 00:02:51.720
If you canceled $10,000 worth of debt

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.540
and especially if you
included an income threshold,

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:57.120
the effects on inflation
would be pretty negligible

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.980
according to most economists.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:00.720
- [Lady] Still some economists say

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.210
there are long term inflationary risks.

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:05.790
- In the long term
student debt forgiveness

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.130
could exacerbate inflationary pressures

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:12.300
by having borrowers treat
loans essentially as Grants

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:16.020
because they expect those
loans to ultimately be forgiven

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.100
by the Federal government.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.767
It could also push up the
price of higher education

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:23.160
because colleges could
pretty truthfully say

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.840
to their perspective students,

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.030
it doesn't really matter
what our tuition costs

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:29.807
because the Federal government
is just gonna forgive

00:03:29.807 --> 00:03:31.020
that debt in the future anyway

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:32.580
- [Lady] In a statement, a spokesperson

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:34.962
for the US Department of Education

00:03:34.962 --> 00:03:37.380
said our overall goal
is long lasting change

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:40.537
that reduces indebtedness and
makes college more affordable

00:03:40.537 --> 00:03:42.904
including through rulemaking.

00:03:42.904 --> 00:03:46.560
Legal challenges may also
complicate the final decision.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.090
According to a legal analysis

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:51.480
prepared by Obama's former top
education department lawyer,

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:53.460
Biden could be on shaky legal ground

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:56.220
if he were to pursue broad-based
student debt cancellation

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.810
by executive action.

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:59.670
- Lots of people including Democrats

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.454
think that they don't have the authority

00:04:01.454 --> 00:04:03.810
to cancel debt on a mass scale

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:07.050
outside of an existing program

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:09.660
like the income based repayment program.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:11.670
And if he just does it
by executive action,

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:13.260
President Biden runs the risk

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:15.270
that this could get overturned in court

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:19.560
especially by a Supreme court
that tilts conservative.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:20.970
- [Lady] Biden has long been skeptical

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:22.500
of using his executive authority

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:23.940
to wipe away student loan debt.

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:26.221
- I don't think I have
the authority to do it

00:04:26.221 --> 00:04:27.054
by sign of a pen.

00:04:27.054 --> 00:04:29.100
- [Lady] Still those
who are financially tied

00:04:30.092 --> 00:04:31.350
to the student loan industry
may be in a position

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:34.830
to sue the administration
like loan servicing companies

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:38.190
and investors that own securities
backed by student loans.

00:04:38.190 --> 00:04:41.010
- So, for instance, the companies
that service these loans

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.047
could potentially sue

00:04:42.047 --> 00:04:44.484
because they would be
servicing fewer loans

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:47.461
because some of those loans
would be forgiven entirely.

00:04:47.461 --> 00:04:51.510
People who hold investments
that are based on the debt

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:54.210
held by these borrowers could also sue

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:56.970
because their underlying
investments would be affected.

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:59.670
- [Lady] If Biden chooses
to go the regulatory route,

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:02.340
there could be other
bureaucratic challenges.

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:06.120
- The issue for Biden if he
goes the regulatory route

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:08.850
is that they haven't really
started a rule making process

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:10.590
for mass debt cancellation,

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:12.991
which means that any
future debt cancellation

00:05:12.991 --> 00:05:15.696
on a mass scale that
went through that process

00:05:15.696 --> 00:05:17.850
would be very far down the road

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:20.307
because of how long the
rulemaking process takes.

00:05:20.307 --> 00:05:22.800
- [Lady] Implementing a
large new government program

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:25.110
may come with logistical hurdles too.

00:05:25.110 --> 00:05:27.120
For instance, a wider forgiveness policy

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:29.790
could require millions of
Americans to file paperwork

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:31.140
detailing their income

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.480
potentially creating a massive backlog.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:36.060
- Canceling debt on this wide of a scale

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:39.390
would be a major logistical
lift for the Federal government.

00:05:39.390 --> 00:05:41.970
They would need to verify people's incomes

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:44.130
if they're putting an
income threshold in place,

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:45.060
they need to make sure

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.830
that they're canceling the right loans

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:48.570
and not canceling others.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.870
And all of that would take a
significant amount of time.

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:52.830
And it's unclear how fast

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:54.300
they would be able to implement it

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:58.170
and whether that would even
happen in Biden's first term.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.640
- [Lady] About 40 million borrowers

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:03.030
hold about 1.6 trillion
in Federal student debt,

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:05.430
making student debt
forgiveness a potent issue

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:07.680
ahead of November's midterm elections,

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:09.660
and a pause on Federal
student loan payments

00:06:09.660 --> 00:06:11.670
is set to expire at the end of August,

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:13.950
just as campaign season gets underway.

00:06:13.950 --> 00:06:17.048
- If Democrats lose
one seat in the Senate,

00:06:17.048 --> 00:06:18.750
they will have lost the majority.

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.833
And if they lose more
than a handful of seats

00:06:20.833 --> 00:06:22.290
in the house of representatives,

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:24.480
they will have lost the
majority there as well

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:27.900
which could badly damage Biden's chances

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:29.760
of enacting anything serious

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:32.610
in the remaining two
years of his first term.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:35.130
- [Lady] Some Democrats
are urging Biden to go big,

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:37.020
hoping that a sweeping
debt forgiveness plan

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:38.700
can motivate voters who will decide

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:40.860
which party controls Congress.

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:43.680
Other Democrats worry such
a move would alienate voters

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:46.163
who don't currently have
student debt or never did.

00:06:46.163 --> 00:06:48.930
At the same time,
Republicans broadly oppose

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:51.480
any type of mass forgiveness policy.

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:54.180
- 40 million people is a major portion

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.620
of the American electorate

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:58.342
making their student debt
payments when they resume

00:06:58.342 --> 00:07:00.600
is going to take a significant chunk

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:01.920
of their income every month.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.770
So it's something that
voters are keenly aware of

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.150
if they hold student debt.

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:08.700
And if they previously
paid off their loans

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.304
or never had loans to begin with,

00:07:10.304 --> 00:07:13.740
they might look at debt
cancellation policies

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.510
and say, well, that wasn't around

00:07:15.510 --> 00:07:17.340
when I was paying for college.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:20.160
- [Lady] As millions of
borrowers await a final decision,

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.980
the Biden administration is
weighing the long term impacts

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.830
of a wide scale student
loan forgiveness program.

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:28.440
- While progressives in
Congress would love for Congress

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:30.600
to do something on
student debt forgiveness,

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.910
they understand that those
votes might not be there

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:35.580
and that nothing is likely
to happen in Congress

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:36.870
at least right now.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.060
So it is up to the Biden administration

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.918
to make these tough calls.

00:07:40.918 --> 00:07:43.501
(upbeat music)

